# Docker build context filter for lab/docker/build.sh (context is the repo
# root). Almost nothing here is COPY'd by infrastructure/containers/Dockerfile
# or Dockerfile.dev, but without this file the full context is still sent to
# the Docker daemon/builder before any COPY filtering happens — including
# whatever local secrets, keys, or evidence bundles happen to exist on the
# machine building the image. See CLAUDE-SECURITY manual review, "docker
# build context" finding.

.git/
# .github/ is COPY'd (see infrastructure/containers/Dockerfile): the in-image
# release-gate tests (tests/unit/test_release_gates.py) assert the GitHub
# Action pin policy against REPO_ROOT/.github/workflows, which only exists in
# the image if the build context actually includes it.

# Local secrets and signed evidence — never send these to any builder,
# local or remote. Mirrors .gitignore's own list.
*.key
*.pem
keys/
secrets/
evidence/
out/
out-*/

# Security review artifacts and other local scratch output.
CLAUDE-SECURITY-*/
.provenance/

# Caches and virtual environments.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Editor/IDE state.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Most documentation is not needed inside the image. The provider policy
# records are an exception: the runtime gate loads them before any probe.
docs/*
!docs/provider-policy-review/
!docs/provider-policy-review/**
examples/
